From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:36:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] d3d12, nvngx: DLSS Super Resolution on D3D12 through
 MetalFX

NGX now has D3D12 entry points. CreateFeature and EvaluateFeature use a new
command list extension, IMTLD3D12CommandListExt, which records a MetalFX
temporal upscale into the command list; the queue plays it back between its
other passes. Motion vectors at output size (no MVLowRes flag) are first
shrunk to render size by a compute pass. Scalers are cached per device and
configuration, like the D3D11 path. Initialisation, parameters, capabilities
and feature release share the D3D11 code.
